        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Section 5.07 (a) All work outside of regular working hours shall be paid at time and one-half the regular rates except Sundays and holidays or days celebrated as such which shall be paid at double time. The holidays are New Year's Day, Memorial Day, Independence Day, Labor Day, Veteran's Day, Thanksgiving Day, the Friday following Thanksgiving Day and Christmas Day. When a holiday falls on a Saturday, Friday will be considered the holiday. When a holiday falls on a Sunday, the following Monday will be considered the holiday. The double time rate will be paid on the holiday and day celebrated as the holiday.",
